# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# s1-conf.allow: the allow-list for the S1 Linux guest configuration,
# orin-native/s1/s1-linux.conf (Phase 3b).
#
# results/orin-native-port/20260909T1100Z/s1-design.md §3.7 (revision 2), with
# owner decisions D13 and D19. D13: S1 has its own allow-list and gate;
# scripts/qhv/g2.conf.allow, which TCR-CFG-001 reviewed for the QNX guest, is
# not edited. D19: one non-GPU FDT overlay may be approved by its sha256.
# `parse-s1.py conf FILE` is the gate; the S1 generators run it at build time.
# The configuration file itself carries no comments, so the bytes the gate
# reads are the bytes every leg stages (§2 rule 2).
#
# Format: one entry per line; '#' starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#
#   <word>                 A configuration keyword. parse-s1.py's grammar says
#                          where each may stand: system, logger, ram, cpu, load,
#                          initrd, cmdline and vdev start a line; hostdev, loc
#                          and intr only follow a vdev line; cluster is only a
#                          cpu option word, and load is also initrd's option
#                          word. A word with no place in that grammar makes the
#                          allow-list itself invalid, and removing a word here
#                          rejects every line that uses it.
#   vdev:<type>            A vdev type the configuration may declare (§2 rule 12).
#   forbid:<word> [<word>] A word, or a sequence of words, that fails the gate
#                          wherever it stands outside the quoted cmdline, also as
#                          a '-', ',', ':' or '='-separated part of a longer
#                          word. The gate refuses an allow-list that drops any
#                          of the six below, or that allows a forbidden word.
#   overlay-sha256:<hex>   D19, at most one. With it, the gate accepts exactly one
#                          line `fdt load /data/s1/<file>` whose PC copy (the
#                          file of that name beside the configuration, or
#                          `conf --overlay FILE`) has this sha256, decodes as an
#                          FDT, names no GPU, SMMU or IOMMU node, property,
#                          label or string, and targets its fragments by path
#                          only (parse-s1.py's overlay screen). The owner's hash
#                          approval stays the primary control. Without it,
#                          `fdt load` is forbidden like the rest (§7.3).
#
# Adding an entry here is a reviewed configuration-surface change.

# --- keywords (§3.7) ---
system
logger
ram
cpu
cluster
load
initrd
cmdline
vdev
hostdev
loc
intr

# --- vdev types: no GPU, pass-through, SMMU, network or block device (§2 rule 12) ---
vdev:pl011
vdev:virtio-console

# --- forbidden (§3.7, §7.3) ---
forbid:pass
forbid:smmu
forbid:fdt load
forbid:virtio-net
forbid:virtio-blk
forbid:shmem

# --- D19: approved non-GPU overlay. None is approved. An approval adds one line
# of this form, and the overlay file is pinned like the configuration:
# overlay-sha256:<64 hex digits>
